{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardti"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comma (≈ 698.045 cents). Four fifths — E→B, B→F♯, A♭→E♭, E♭→B♭ — are each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma, equal to the equal-temperament fifth"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2^(7\/12) ≈ 700.000 cents. The remaining four fifths are pure. The circle closes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly: 4×(1\/6) + 4×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Neidhardt relabeled this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"specification “Small City” in his 1732 revision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ivo